  "configuration_id": "config_035",
  "reason": "The best result so far is config_036 (scvi_n200, imagenet_vit_l, avgpool, weighted) at 0.706 accuracy. For pca_n2000, aggregation had a large effect (avgpool 0.635 vs transformer 0.599, ~3.6% gap), but scvi_n200 produces a fundamentally different 200-dim learned latent representation that may interact differently with transformer aggregation. Config_035 tests a single-variable change (avgpool→transformer) from the best config while keeping the proven scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + weighted combination. If transformer aggregation captures cross-modal relationships better in the lower-dimensional scvi space, it could push accuracy above 0.706; if not, it confirms avgpool is optimal and directs remaining budget toward other variables (e.g., image encoder). This is the highest-information experiment for reducing uncertainty around the current best configuration with 4 experiments still remaining."
}

